      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "- Used to connect multiple micro services together\n- Language agnostic\n- Uses Protocol buffer to define contract of the data shared between services\n- Protobuf, which is short for “Protocol Buffers,” is an efficient, language-agnostic data serialization mechanism. \nIt enables developers to define structured data in a .proto file, which is then used to generate source code \nthat can write and read data from different data streams.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Used to connect multiple micro services together\n- Language agnostic\n- Uses Protocol buffer to define contract of the data shared between services\n- Protobuf, which is short for “Protocol Buffers,” is an efficient, language-agnostic data serialization mechanism. \nIt enables developers to define structured data in a .proto file, which is then used to generate source code \nthat can write and read data from different data streams.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
