      "fontSize": 37.93971943684054,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "- Used to connect client and server\n- Client and server should use Typescript\n- Unlike REST, which often requires extensive boilerplate for defining routes and handling serialization, or \nGraphQL, which requires schema definitions and resolvers, \ntRPC leverages TypeScript to define APIs with end-to-end type safety.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Used to connect client and server\n- Client and server should use Typescript\n- Unlike REST, which often requires extensive boilerplate for defining routes and handling serialization, or \nGraphQL, which requires schema definitions and resolvers, \ntRPC leverages TypeScript to define APIs with end-to-end type safety.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
