      "fontSize": 36,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "- A webhook is an HTTP request, triggered by an event in a source system and \nsent to a destination system, often with a payload of data. \n- Webhooks are automated, in other words they are automatically sent out when their event is fired in the source system.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- A webhook is an HTTP request, triggered by an event in a source system and \nsent to a destination system, often with a payload of data. \n- Webhooks are automated, in other words they are automatically sent out when their event is fired in the source system.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
