      "updated": 1728357780461,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 62.27840317464227,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "- Gzip and Brotli are the most common ways to compress JavaScript and are widely supported by modern browsers.\n- Brotli offers a better compression ratio at similar compression levels.\n- Next.js provides Gzip compression by default but recommends enabling it on an HTTP proxy like Nginx.\n- If you use Webpack to bundle your code, you can use the CompressionPlugin for Gzip compression or the BrotliWebpackPlugin for Brotli compression.\n- Oyo saw a 15-20% reduction, and Wix saw a 21-25% reduction in file sizes after switching to Brotli compression instead of Gzip.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "- Gzip and Brotli are the most common ways to compress JavaScript and are widely supported by modern browsers.\n- Brotli offers a better compression ratio at similar compression levels.\n- Next.js provides Gzip compression by default but recommends enabling it on an HTTP proxy like Nginx.\n- If you use Webpack to bundle your code, you can use the CompressionPlugin for Gzip compression or the BrotliWebpackPlugin for Brotli compression.\n- Oyo saw a 15-20% reduction, and Wix saw a 21-25% reduction in file sizes after switching to Brotli compression instead of Gzip.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
