      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1728008780049,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 32.571428571428974,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "text": "-Besides user interaction, we often have components that aren’t visible on the initial page.\n- A good example of this is lazy loading images that aren’t directly visible in the viewport, but only get loaded once the user scrolls down.\n- We can do the same with components! In order to know whether components are currently in our viewport, we can use the IntersectionObserver API, \nor use libraries such as react-lazyload or react-loadable-visibility to quickly add import on visibility to our application.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "-Besides user interaction, we often have components that aren’t visible on the initial page.\n- A good example of this is lazy loading images that aren’t directly visible in the viewport, but only get loaded once the user scrolls down.\n- We can do the same with components! In order to know whether components are currently in our viewport, we can use the IntersectionObserver API, \nor use libraries such as react-lazyload or react-loadable-visibility to quickly add import on visibility to our application.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
